  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# iiVoiceOver\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "iiVoiceOver"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "A C++23 PCM audio API with explicit availability reporting for speech synthesis.\nThe previous Piper/ONNX learned voice backend and its bundled voice are retired.\n`SpeechSynthesizer::available()` returns false; `VoiceModel::load()` and `bundled()`\nreport unsupported model inference. No model or native inference runtime is\nautomatically downloaded.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 8,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 9,
      "end_line": 14,
      "raw": "`SpeechAudio` retains owned float32 PCM, duration calculation, and validated\nPCM16 WAV encoding through `waveBytes()`. The independent SDK does not link\nother SDKs. An application can compose it with iiFileProvider using the\nseparately configured [file consumer](examples/file-provider), which publishes\nexclusively and never overwrites an existing destination. PCM encoding does not\nrequire a learned model.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 15,
      "end_line": 15,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 16,
      "end_line": 18,
      "raw": "`Result` and `ErrorCode` now belong to `iiVoiceOver` rather than iiSDKCore.\nThe `SpeechAudio::saveWave(path)` member was removed: migrate to the consumer\nadapter or publish `waveBytes()` in the application, and rebuild callers.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 19,
      "end_line": 19,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "fenced_code",
      "start_line": 20,
      "end_line": 24,
      "raw": "```sh\ncmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_TESTING=ON\ncmake --build build --parallel 2\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n```\n",
      "language": "sh",
      "code": "cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_TESTING=ON\ncmake --build build --parallel 2\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n",
      "closed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b000010",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 25,
      "end_line": 25,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 26,
      "end_line": 29,
      "raw": "The [native CLI](examples/native-cli) is a separate consumer of iiVoiceOver,\niiSDKCore and iiFileProvider. It reports `synthesisAvailable` and\n`pcmExportAvailable`. A speech request fails explicitly until a separate\nsupported native backend is implemented.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000012",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 30,
      "end_line": 30,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 31,
      "end_line": 33,
      "raw": "See [the runtime retirement contract](docs/RuntimeRetirement.md) and the public\nAPI in `src/iiVoiceOver.h`. Historical Piper licensing records do not describe a\nruntime included in current builds.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000014",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 34,
      "end_line": 34,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000015",
      "kind": "html",
      "start_line": 35,
      "end_line": 35,
      "raw": "<!-- workspace-docs:readme:start -->\n"
    },
